#: ../../faq.rst
msgid "Q: How do I install Spyder on Windows Subsystem for Linux 2 (WSL2)?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../faq.rst:27
msgid "If you already installed Spyder on your Windows machine, you do not need to reinstall it on a WSL2-based Linux environment to run your code there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../faq.rst:30
msgid "Instead, create a new Conda environment (with ``conda create -n my-env -c conda-forge python``) or venv/virtualenv (with e.g. ``python -m venv .my-env``), activate it (``conda activate my-env`` or ``source .my-env/bin/activate``) and then install Spyder-Kernels into that environment (with ``conda install -c conda-forge spyder-kernels`` or ``pip install spyder-kernels``, respectively)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../faq.rst:34
msgid "Using system Python without a virtual environment is **not** recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../faq.rst:38
msgid "Windows creates a network path located at ``\\\\wsl$`` that points to the partitions of your WSL2 machines, e.g. ``\\\\wsl$\\Ubuntu-20.04``. You **must** map a network drive letter to your machine path, e.g. ``W:``, for Spyder to correctly see its files and folders."
msgstr ""

