#: ../../faq.rst
msgid "Q: What are the system requirements for Spyder? How resource-intensive is it?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../faq.rst:138
msgid "Spyder works on modern versions of Windows, macOS and Linux (see the table below for recommended versions). It typically uses relatively minimal CPU when idle, and 0.5 GB - 1 GB of RAM, depending on how long you've been using it and how many files, projects, panes and consoles you have open. It should work on any system with a dual-core or better x64 processor and at least 4 GB of RAM, although 8 GB is *strongly* recommended for best performance when running other applications. The code you run, such as scientific computations and deep learning models, may require additional resources beyond this baseline for Spyder itself."
msgstr ""

